// Regicide - opening Isafdar cutscene: Idris tries to warn the player and is killed by
// Essyllt and Morvran (checklist item #6).
//
// NPC identities confirmed directly from their [name=] fields in scripts/_unpack/377/all.npc
// (not a guess): regicide_good_elf1 = "Idris", regicide_evil_elf1 = "Essyllt",
// regicide_evil_elf2 = "Morvran". regicide_good_elf3 = "Arianwyn" (the elf who intercepts the
// sealed letter in the ending, step 12 - not used here, noted for whoever builds that later).
//
// Trigger choice: talking to Idris directly (op1=Talk-to on regicide_good_elf1), not a loc/entry
// trigger - the Isafdar map locs aren't migrated out of _unpack yet (same situation
// regicide_isafdar_obstacles.rs2 already lives with), so there's no real loc to hook an
// oploc/entry trigger off of. Talking to Idris is the simpler, equally-faithful trigger per the
// walkthrough ("an elf, Idris, tries to talk to you").
//
// Essyllt/Morvran are voiced via the secondary active-npc slot (.npc_find + ~.chatnpc), the same
// pattern quest_arena/scripts/fightslave.rs2 and several other quests already use for a second
// NPC to speak by name mid-scene. Idris's death is narrated, not a real combat calculation - he
// plays human_death (the generic seq every human-skeleton npc in this codebase reuses, including
// these elf models per their own walkanim=human_walk_*/readyanim=human_ready) and is removed with
// npc_del. This is intentionally a modest, narrated moment, not a scripted fight engine.

[opnpc1,regicide_good_elf1]
if(%regicide_quest < ^regicide_started) {
    mes("The elf glances at you warily but says nothing.");
    return;
}
if(%regicide_quest > ^regicide_started) {
    mes("There is no sign of the elf now.");
    return;
}
~chatnpc("<p,worried>Wait, traveller - you must not go any further. Iorwerth's men are watching this path, and if they find you...");
if(.npc_find(npc_coord, regicide_evil_elf1, 10, 0) = true) {
    .npc_facesquare(npc_coord);
    ~.chatnpc("<p,angry>Idris! You dare speak to an outsider?");
}
~chatplayer("<p,shock>What's going on?");
if(.npc_find(npc_coord, regicide_evil_elf2, 10, 0) = true) {
    ~.chatnpc("<p,angry>Lord Iorwerth's law is absolute. Traitors share the same fate as spies.");
}
mes("Before Idris can say another word, Essyllt and Morvran cut him down.");
npc_anim(human_death, 0);
p_delay(1);
npc_del;
if(.npc_find(coord, regicide_evil_elf1, 10, 0) = true) {
    .npc_facesquare(coord);
    ~.chatnpc("<p,angry>You saw nothing here. Go to Lord Iorwerth at his camp, in the north-west, and pray he's more merciful than we are.");
} else {
    ~mesbox("Shaken, you realise your only option now is to find Lord Iorwerth at his camp to the north-west.");
}
%regicide_quest = ^regicide_met_elves;
